## Q4: hedging

Does hedging (a second request after the p95 delay) cut the tail, and at
what cost in extra requests? Command: `make bench-hedge`
(`eval/hedge/run.sh`), raw files in `eval/results/q4-hedge/`.
{{with .Q4}}
**Method.** The fake provider runs as its own process. Each request's first
byte comes after a log-normal delay with median {{.Meta.FakeProvider.Latency}} (σ = {{.Sigma}}), and an
independent {{.SlowPercent}}% of requests are {{.Meta.FakeProvider.SlowFactor}}× slower; then {{.Meta.FakeProvider.Tokens}} tokens follow
{{.Meta.FakeProvider.TokenInterval}} apart. `switchboard bench` offers {{.Meta.Rate}} streamed requests per second
through the gateway for {{.Meta.Duration}} after a {{.Meta.Warmup}} warm-up, open loop (latency from
the scheduled time), once with hedging off and once with it on. Each arm
starts a fresh gateway, so the hedge delay is learned from the run's own
